// CMKFC

@0    = ~Welcome to my fine establishment. Can I get you today's special?~
@1    = ~Special? What special is that?~
@2    = ~No I am not interested in the special. I'm just looking around.~
@3    = ~Come back any time.~
@4    = ~The special today is our mouth watering, slow roasted chicken with our secret 20 herbs and spices. It also comes with mashed potatoes covered in our special gravy. Would you like to try some?~
@5    = ~Sounds good to me. I'll take the special and let me see what else is on the menu.~
@6    = ~No I am not interested in the special. I am just looking around.~
@7    = ~Ok here you go. Enjoy.~

// DOS

@0     = ~Bienvenue dans mon bel établissement. Puis-je vous proposer la spécialité du jour ?~
@1     = ~Spécialité ? Qu'a-t-elle de spécial ?~
@2     = ~Non merci, je ne suis pas intéressé. Je jette juste un coup d'oeil.~
         ~Non merci, je ne suis pas intéressée. Je jette juste un coup d'oeil.~
@3     = ~Revenez quand vous voulez.~
@4     = ~La spécialité du jour est notre appétissant poulet rôti à feu doux assaisonné de notre sélection de 20 herbes et épices. Il est accompagné de purée de pommes de terre recouverte de notre sauce maison. Aimeriez-vous y goûter ?~
@5     = ~Ca me plait. Je prendrai la spécialité mais laissez-moi voir ce qu'il y a d'autre au menu.~
@6     = ~Non merci, je ne suis pas intéressé. Je jette juste un coup d'oeil.~
         ~Non merci, je ne suis pas intéressée. Je jette juste un coup d'oeil.~
@7     = ~C'est parti. Bon appétit.~


//////////////////


@8    = ~Greetings traveler. You have the look of an adventurer who has seen many miles of travel and encounters. I was wondering if you could help me out with a problem.~
@9    = ~We might be able to help you, what is the problem?~
@10   = ~Sorry we do not have the time.~
@11   = ~Well one night when I was staying at one of the inns here in Amn and a thief took my Tome of Magic. This book I need returned to me as soon as soon as possible. I was bringing this book to Candlekeep... oh dear the High Priestess will be so upset with me. Can you help me out?~
@12   = ~Sure we can. Do you have any details on the thief that took this book of yours?~
@13   = ~Well thanks anyway.~
@14   = ~I do not know anything about the thief but I suspect the thief was working for a Priestess of Shar. They have been following me since I left my church days ago. I saw one of their guards recently at the Five Flagons Inn if that would help you.~
@15   = ~We'll start from there and return if we find out anything new.~
@16   = ~I see you have returned. Do you have my magical tome?~
@17   = ~No we do not.~
@18   = ~Please hurry up and return when you have it.~
@19   = ~You return and have my tome. I am most grateful for this. For this I'll give you 1000 gold and access to my store while I am here.~
@20   = ~Glad to see you <CHARNAME> what can I do for you?~
@21   = ~Lets see what you have in your store.~
@22   = ~Nothing.~
@23   = ~Ok here is what I have.~
@24   = ~Return if you change your mind.~


//////////////////

// CMNINAST


@25   = ~Good business, my <LADYLORD>.  I don't think I've seen you before... perhaps you might be interested in looking at some well-priced goods that have fallen into my hands?~
@26   = ~Are you trying to tell me that these goods are stolen?~
@27   = ~Sure, let me see what you have.~
@28   = ~No, I'm not interested in anything.~
@29   = ~I don't think of them as stolen, my <LADYLORD>. Merely 'previously owned'. And, truly, the ease of which I acquired them could truly be called akin to merely 'falling' into my hands.~
@30   = ~Well, I'll have no qualms about it.  Let me see what you have to offer.~
@31   = ~Not interested.~
@32   = ~A most prudent choice, and one you'll quickly see is worth your while.~
@33   = ~That is too bad, my <LADYLORD>. Perhaps you are in need of a few coppers? Or shall I find you some swaddling clothes?~
@34   = ~Ah!  It is good to see you again, my <LADYLORD>. Might you be interested in perusing some goods that have fallen into my hands?~
@35   = ~You are selling stolen goods?~
@36   = ~Yes, let me see what you have.~
@37   = ~No, thanks.~

